# Shipped as .gitignore in the public repo (renamed when the seed is built).
#
# Kept separate from this repo's own .gitignore, which also excludes things
# specific to the maintainer's machine. This file must stay generic: it is the
# first line of defence for everyone who clones SUNI, and the reason the
# original repo ended up tracking secrets was that these rules arrived after
# the files did.

# ── Instance state — never commit ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything SUNI generates at runtime: databases, memory stores, the document
# index, uploads, and the secrets it creates for itself on first run.
#
# LEADING SLASH MATTERS. A bare "memory/" matches at ANY depth, so it also
# ignores the suni/memory/ PACKAGE — which is how the first release shipped
# without its memory manager, store and consolidator. Anchor every state
# directory to the repository root.
/memory/
/logs/
/backups/
/files/

# ── Credentials ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
/certs/

# ── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# ── Editors / OS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
